            "treatment.3",
            "diagnosis_background.0"
          ],
          "text": "Background risk factors included maternal GBS positivity in this pregnancy and intrapartum antibiotics administered less than 4 hours before delivery. A septic screen was performed; CRP rose from 28 to 41 on Day 1 before falling to 18 on Day 2. Blood culture showed no growth at 36 hours and was confirmed negative at 48 hours. Lumbar puncture was deferred given stable respiratory status. In view of the clinical picture and initial CRP rise, a decision was made to complete a 5-day course of IV benzylpenicillin and gentamicin per neonatal sepsis protocol; antibiotics were completed on 20/05. Routine newborn checks were performed and the newborn hearing screen was passed.",
